                hi: 15,
            },
            label: "wolf's bitwise not is `!`",
        },
        secondary: [],
        notes: [
            "`!` on an integer is its bitwise complement at the operand's own width ([type.int.not]): `!x` for `~x`, and `e & !m` clears the bits of `m`. wolf spells it `!` by ruling and has no `~` operator.",
        ],
        suggestions: [
            Suggestion {
                message: "write `!` for the bitwise not",
